%N A398335 Number of strongly connected digraphs on n labeled nodes that are acyclic after deleting node 1.
%C A398335 All digraphs are loopless. Equivalently, choose an acyclic digraph A on nodes 2,...,n and subsets S and R of its nodes. Add node 1 and the edges 1 -> v for v in S and v -> 1 for v in R. The resulting digraph is strongly connected if and only if S contains every source of A and R contains every sink of A. A source has in-degree 0 and a sink has out-degree 0.
%C A398335 Thus each A contributes 2^(n-1-sources(A)) * 2^(n-1-sinks(A)) choices. The empty A gives a(1) = 1. Node 1 is fixed, not chosen as an additional part of the structure.
%D A398335 A. V. Aho, M. S. Lam, R. Sethi and J. D. Ullman, Compilers: Principles, Techniques, and Tools, 2nd ed., Addison-Wesley, 2006, Section 9.7 (reducible flow graphs).
%D A398335 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%H A398335 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A398335/b398335.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..76</a>
%H A398335 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A398335/a398335.py.txt">Python program</a>, Oct 2026.
%F A398335 a(n) = Sum_{DAGs A on n-1 labeled nodes} 2^(n-1-sources(A)) * 2^(n-1-sinks(A)).
%F A398335 a(n) = Sum_{k,l} T(n-1,k,l) * 2^(n-1-k) * 2^(n-1-l) with T the joint distribution of labeled DAGs by number of sources and sinks.
%o A398335 (Python) [count_labeled_flat_strong(n) for n in range(1, 15)] # See link for program code.
%o A398335 (Python) everywhere_reducible_sequence("labeled_flat_strong", 20) # See Python link in A400123 for program code.
%Y A398335 Cf. A003024 (labeled DAGs), A003030 (strong digraphs), A350415.
